WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:01.399
- If you are Googling about diet,

00:00:01.399 --> 00:00:03.802
understand that even though
it's the information age,

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:06.552
I call it the misinformation age.

00:00:10.466 --> 00:00:11.857
- My name is LeeAnn Weintraub.

00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:14.499
I'm a registered dietician in Los Angeles.

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:15.649
- My name is Kevin Libby.

00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:17.644
I'm a nutritionist for PH2 Nutrition.

00:00:17.644 --> 00:00:20.272
- And I provide nutrition
counseling and consulting services

00:00:20.272 --> 00:00:23.589
to adults, families,
businesses, and organizations.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.910
- Today, we're gonna be
answering Googled questions

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:26.827
about diet.

00:00:29.927 --> 00:00:31.779
- Registered dieticians like myself

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:33.638
are food and nutrition experts

00:00:33.638 --> 00:00:36.074
but we're not always big fans of diets.

00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:38.977
Diets often don't work,
people fail at diets,

00:00:38.977 --> 00:00:41.127
and then, there's this kind of sad feeling

00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:42.831
of failure that comes along with that.

00:00:42.831 --> 00:00:44.296
- The word diet in general.

00:00:44.296 --> 00:00:46.566
It's got a connotation to
it that is like, you know,

00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:47.857
people have to deal with restriction.

00:00:47.857 --> 00:00:50.225
And I have my own saying,
it's not about restriction,

00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:51.339
it's about consistency.

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:53.691
- So, my approach is more
of a lifestyle approach

00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:55.973
that focuses on balance, portion control,

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:59.390
eating healthy nutrient-dense whole food.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:02.807
If you're following a
diet and you're wondering

00:01:02.807 --> 00:01:04.628
if you can have a cheat day, the answer is

00:01:04.628 --> 00:01:05.464
- Maybe.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.771
The leaner you are, the
bigger cheat you can have.

00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:10.157
The heavier you are, the
more it's a bad idea.

00:01:10.157 --> 00:01:11.985
- I would actually recommend look at more

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:13.144
like a splurge meal.

00:01:13.144 --> 00:01:15.860
So a meal once a week, maybe twice

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.920
where you're kind of
looking forward to that,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.187
maybe indulging in something

00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:22.020
that's a little bit off your plan.

00:01:25.355 --> 00:01:27.268
I would say you wanna
be careful with that.

00:01:27.268 --> 00:01:29.515
There's benefits to a lot
of the healthy food groups

00:01:29.515 --> 00:01:32.033
like grains, like dairy products.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.227
And unless you have a food
allergy or a food sensitivity,

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.352
most of us need these healthy food groups

00:01:37.352 --> 00:01:40.649
for the micronutrients and the
macronutrients that we need.

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:41.859
- If you remove carbohydrates,

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:43.535
you'll deplete glycogen storage.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:46.878
Your body will be forced
to utilize fat for fuel

00:01:46.878 --> 00:01:48.531
but you can't under-calorie.

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:50.474
You don't wanna restrict
calories too much.

00:01:50.474 --> 00:01:51.422
- You wanna think about

00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:53.519
maybe getting the right
amount for your body

00:01:53.519 --> 00:01:55.515
which often involves portion control

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.848
and cutting back the excess.

00:01:59.914 --> 00:02:02.396
- In America, we've overstated
protein way too much.

00:02:02.396 --> 00:02:04.165
Concentrated proteins
will still spike insulin.

00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:06.444
- Your body needs a balance
of all the macronutrients.

00:02:06.444 --> 00:02:09.516
The amount of calories,
carbohydrates, protein and fats

00:02:09.516 --> 00:02:11.704
that you need in your daily nutrition plan

00:02:11.704 --> 00:02:13.619
really varies from person to person.

00:02:13.619 --> 00:02:14.865
- It's not just protein.

00:02:14.865 --> 00:02:16.152
You have to break down the tissue

00:02:16.152 --> 00:02:17.892
by working out really, really hard

00:02:17.892 --> 00:02:19.114
with really heavy weight

00:02:19.114 --> 00:02:21.482
but you also need carbohydrate
to fuel the training.

00:02:21.482 --> 00:02:23.082
- And it's not the same for everybody.

00:02:23.082 --> 00:02:25.276
So you want to focus on a
plan that works for you.

00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:28.117
And speaking with an expert
such as a registered dietician

00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:31.017
or your physician is gonna
give you the best approach

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.899
and the best advice that you
need to reach your goals.

00:02:33.899 --> 00:02:36.094
- So we just answered
the questions about diet.

00:02:36.094 --> 00:02:38.463
So the most important thing
to take away from this is

00:02:38.463 --> 00:02:41.389
- It's all about making
healthy, balanced eating choices

00:02:41.389 --> 00:02:43.704
that make sense for your
lifestyle and your body.

00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:46.715
- We wanna go organic, we wanna
stay away from refined oils,

00:02:46.715 --> 00:02:48.445
we wanna stay away from GMOs.

00:02:48.445 --> 00:02:49.653
- These are really important things

00:02:49.653 --> 00:02:51.123
to get the right answer on

00:02:51.123 --> 00:02:53.806
and we know that Google
doesn't have all the answers.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.189
And if you meet with an expert,

00:02:55.189 --> 00:02:57.889
you get information and advice
that's customized to you.

00:02:57.889 --> 00:02:58.877
- Don't overthink it, you know,

00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:00.599
people are way too obsessed with it.

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:03.081
Don't sweat the petty stuff
and don't pet the sweaty stuff.

00:03:03.081 --> 00:03:05.664
(upbeat music)

